      "words": 96,
      "text": "Does the prime minister recall that at the time after he became prime minister under the coalition and at the time when he was dividing the nation between strivers and skroungers? I asked him a very important question about the windfall he received when he wrote off the mortgage of the premises in Notting Hill. And I said to him, he didn't write off the mortgage of the one the taxpayers were helping to pay for at Oxford. I didn't receive a proper answer then. Maybe dodgy Dave will answer it now. And by the way",
